[[31,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p><a href=\"#/3025840\">7045A10</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025842\">7045A25</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025855\">7045A84</a></p><p>1. Remove the heater pad, detaching it from the squab padding.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2005413.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[31,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Check that the heater pad is\nnot damaged.</p><p>1. Place the heater pad (1a) in its original position and attach\nthe adhesive side to the padding.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>position the electrical wire in\ngroove (1b) and take it round behind the padding.</p></aside><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2005414.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[31,63,0,"<p><a href=\"#/3025855\">7045A84</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025842\">7045A25</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025840\">7045A10</a></p>"]]